olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The jump in government borrowing costs thi=
s year is causing concern at the International Monetary Fund, as policymake=
rs gather in Bangkok for its annual meeting.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In its fiscal monitor report, released thi=
s morning, the IMF is warning that the rise in sovereign bond yields has =
=E2=80=9Craised the fiscal stakes=E2=80=9D facing governments, as they try =
to keep borrowing under control.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Higher borrowing costs are adding to fisca=
l pressures at a time of high debt, making credible consolidation more urge=
nt, it points out.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It is demanding action, saying: =E2=80=9CT=
he more countries wait, the more painful the adjustment becomes.=E2=80=9D</=
p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This is easier said than done, though. Fra=
nce, for example, faces a struggle to push through a budget that would only=
 cut its annual deficit to 5% of GDP. In the UK the chancellor, John Healey=
, could face a battle with his own MPs if he proposes welfare cuts in his b=
udget later this month.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The IMF points out that since February =E2=
=80=93 when the Iran war began and oil prices jumped =E2=80=93 the average =
10-year government bond yield for G7 countries increased by more than one p=
ercentage point, reaching its highest level in almost two decades.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Bank of England governor, Andrew Baile=
y, and the IMF managing director, Kristalina Georgieva, have issued a stark=
 warning about the growing risks of cyber-attacks.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Georgieva cited her childhood growing up i=
n eastern Europe, when wary citizens did not trust the system, so kept thei=
r money in a shoebox under the bed.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">She said: =E2=80=9CWhat I worry, today, is=
 that unless we figure out how to get ahead of this curve, given the speed,=
 the scale and the cost of fraud growing up, we may end up with lots of peo=
ple with shoeboxes under their beds.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Bailey agreed, citing a warning from Anthr=
opic this week that rogue AI agents <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.the=
guardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEA13-uHzzNL=
sl3ZqJFCJlFepJihajm4E2D-6UaDsnPnQz6xJMDTpSd1vkByrym3Jv6Be_G8TiqvzuQElO15xBi=
